[2026-03-15T00:50:22.791Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019vTCsoFPfVAqA51C5nQA9Y","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\n**Replay MCP** is a tool for investigating recordings from https://replay.io. It captures complete browser sessions, allowing you to analyze app behavior with forensic precision.\n\n## Core Concept\n\n\"The recording is essentially a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed.\" Key terms include:\n\n- **Point**: A specific execution moment when JS statements run or events occur\n- **Element**: A DOM element reference independent of particular points\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe documentation recommends a structured approach:\n\n1. Frame your investigation as a specific question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Develop and test hypotheses with gathered data\n5. Support conclusions with evidence\n\n## Available Tools\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what happened:\n- Error tracking (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline views (console, storage, network, React renders)\n- Source code inspection with hit counts\n\n**Explanatory Tools** explain why it happened:\n- Stack traces and control dependencies\n- Point descriptions and variable inspection\n- React component trees and expression evaluation\n\n## Key Recommendation\n\n\"The Logpoint tool is extremely useful for this: see the value of the same expression whenever a statement executed, look for anything unexpected, and continue investigating from there.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30bc8576-b4c8-496e-a563-b403a6d12d18","uuid":"b21b20f8-6787-458a-8cda-6b2062a99930","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\n**Replay MCP** is a tool for investigating recordings from https://replay.io. It captures complete browser sessions, allowing you to analyze app behavior with forensic precision.\n\n## Core Concept\n\n\"The recording is essentially a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed.\" Key terms include:\n\n- **Point**: A specific execution moment when JS statements run or events occur\n- **Element**: A DOM element reference independent of particular points\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe documentation recommends a structured approach:\n\n1. Frame your investigation as a specific question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Develop and test hypotheses with gathered data\n5. Support conclusions with evidence\n\n## Available Tools\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what happened:\n- Error tracking (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline views (console, storage, network, React renders)\n- Source code inspection with hit counts\n\n**Explanatory Tools** explain why it happened:\n- Stack traces and control dependencies\n- Point descriptions and variable inspection\n- React component trees and expression evaluation\n\n## Key Recommendation\n\n\"The Logpoint tool is extremely useful for this: see the value of the same expression whenever a statement executed, look for anything unexpected, and continue investigating from there.\"","durationMs":2921,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T00:50:23.312Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7gnXgfLgC2JNEwUxgxCTB","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Documentation\n\n## Overview\n\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It allows users to install the CLI, record sessions, upload recordings, and manage them.\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall globally using your preferred package manager:\n- npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun all support installation with the `i -g replayio` command syntax\n\n## Authentication\n\nUsers should navigate to https://app.replay.io settings, create an API key, and store it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\nThe tool provides commands for:\n- **Recording**: Launch the Replay Browser and capture sessions at a specified URL\n- **Uploading**: Submit recorded sessions using recording IDs\n- **Management**: List local recordings or remove them individually or in bulk\n- **Authentication**: Login/logout functionality for account access\n- **Utilities**: Check installation info, update components, and access help documentation\n\n## Workflow Example\n\nUsers typically start by running `replayio record [url]` to launch the browser and begin capturing. After recording concludes, they can upload using the recording ID via `replayio upload [id]`.\n\n## Additional Features\n\nThe CLI supports source map uploads for workspaces and integrates with an MCP server for debugging recorded applications through Claude with proper authorization headers."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30bc8576-b4c8-496e-a563-b403a6d12d18","uuid":"4d8aa509-3cae-4937-aa17-66e85a9f90ab","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Documentation\n\n## Overview\n\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It allows users to install the CLI, record sessions, upload recordings, and manage them.\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall globally using your preferred package manager:\n- npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun all support installation with the `i -g replayio` command syntax\n\n## Authentication\n\nUsers should navigate to https://app.replay.io settings, create an API key, and store it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\nThe tool provides commands for:\n- **Recording**: Launch the Replay Browser and capture sessions at a specified URL\n- **Uploading**: Submit recorded sessions using recording IDs\n- **Management**: List local recordings or remove them individually or in bulk\n- **Authentication**: Login/logout functionality for account access\n- **Utilities**: Check installation info, update components, and access help documentation\n\n## Workflow Example\n\nUsers typically start by running `replayio record [url]` to launch the browser and begin capturing. After recording concludes, they can upload using the recording ID via `replayio upload [id]`.\n\n## Additional Features\n\nThe CLI supports source map uploads for workspaces and integrates with an MCP server for debugging recorded applications through Claude with proper authorization headers.","durationMs":4336,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
